## Critical Constraints — Never Break These
- **Drupal core is locked to `~10.6.3`** by the Satellite profile (`esn/satellite-profile 5.1.1`). Do not update Drupal core until a new Satellite version supports it. Security coverage ends December 2026.
- **Radix theme must stay at `^5.0`**. Radix 6.x breaks every page with a 503 error because the Satellite theme templates reference `@radix/form/input.twig` which doesn't exist in Radix 6. Drupal will show an "unsupported release" warning — ignore it.
- **Never use the Drupal admin UI updater**. It partially downloads files and corrupts the codebase. Always update via `composer update` in the terminal.
- **Never edit `web/sites/*/settings.php` directly**. Always edit `scaffold/*.settings.php` then run `composer drupal:scaffold`. Settings files need `sudo chmod u+w` before scaffold can overwrite them.

## Scaffold System
Settings files are managed via a scaffold system:
- Source files: `scaffold/*.settings.php` (one per site)
- Pushed to `web/sites/*/settings.php` via `composer drupal:scaffold`
- `sites.php` source is at `scaffold/sites.php`
- To update a settings file:
  1. `sudo chmod u+w web/sites/DOMAIN/settings.php`
  2. Edit `scaffold/DOMAIN.settings.php`
  3. `composer drupal:scaffold`
  4. `vendor/bin/drush --uri=https://DOMAIN cr`

## File Permissions Important Notes
- After any `composer update`, new files may be created as `rw-rw----` (no world-readable). Section site PHP-FPM workers run as different users (e.g. `esn-mate`) and can't read them, causing 500 errors.
- Fix with: `find /home/esn-hungary/htdocs/new-hungary.esn.hu/vendor -type f -exec chmod o+r {} \;` and `find /home/esn-hungary/htdocs/new-hungary.esn.hu/vendor -type d -exec chmod o+rx {} \;`
- After `composer update`, always fix vendor permissions if section sites show 500 errors.

